    "body": "Fix #39394\r\n\r\n### Problem\r\n\r\n`:cabbrev` replaces abbreviations anywhere in the cmdline, causing unwanted expansions when the abbreviated word appears as an argument rather than a command:\r\n\r\n```vim\r\n:cabbrev x y\r\n:cmd x    \" expands to :cmd y - unwanted\r\n```\r\n\r\n### Solution\r\n\r\nIntroduce a fourth abbreviation type identified by a `:` prefix on the LHS:\r\n\r\n```vim\r\n:cabbrev :man :Man\r\n```\r\n\r\n`:` prefix abbreviations only expand when the word appears at command position, which is either the start of the cmdline or after a `|`. Regular abbreviations are unchanged.\r\n\r\nTwo fields are added to `mapblock_T`: `is_cmd_abbr` and `cmdidx`. `map_add` strips the `:` prefix, resolves `cmdidx` via `find_ex_command`, and sets `is_cmd_abbr`. `check_abbr` matches `:` prefix abbreviations by `cmdidx` at command position rather than by string comparison.\r\n\r\nHandles `[range]` and standard cmdline modifiers:\r\n\r\n`:cabbrev :grep :& grep`\r\n- `:gr` to `:& grep`\r\n- `:1,2gr` to `:& 1,2grep`\r\n- `:echo gr | 1,2gr` to `:echo gr | & 1,2grep`\r\n- `:!gr` to `:& !gr`",
